# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------
# the generator's rocks that floated over the slope, and walls left wholly under the ground (ground check, 2026-10-23)
clear at -15.01 5.23 r=1.5 only=SmallBoulder

info title=Biome Seven
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A glass garden dome 18 m down, its air still in: crop beds, a mango tree, a caged lab goat - and outside, rays at the vent and a giant puffer. The fourth island of The Sunken Kingdom.
island on.arrive=message||A buoy - and far below it, a glass dome on the seabed, lit from inside.

story cycled|Airlock cycled|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|You opened Biome Seven's airlock hatch.
story melonseed|Melon seed packet|Seed_Watermelon|A packet of melon seeds from Biome Seven's beds.
story watered|Beds watered|Placeable_Sprinkler|You turned the sprinkler crank: Biome Seven's beds are green again.

note hydrolog Hydrophone log | HYDROPHONE LOG - BIOME SEVEN (printout, W. Ashby's pencil in the margin)\n\n03:10 Low call, bearing out past the reef, the trench. Not whale. Not ship.\n03:12 Same. Closer.\n03:40 The call has changed. It is copying the dome's beacon - the same two notes, the same gap.\n04:05 It is copying the Network's line tone now. On the speaker it sounds almost like a word. "Calling. Calling."\n04:30 Teal light outside the glass. It waited by the airlock for nine minutes. Then it went towards the lab tower, against the current.\n\nMargin: "It doesn't hunt by eye. It hunts by what is LIT and what is LOUD. Told the Director. He said thank you, Wren, that is very useful, and the line went dead."
note wrenletter Wren's letter | WREN ASHBY - LETTER, IN A TIN UNDER THE BEDS\n\nWhoever turned my sprinklers on: thank you. The melons thank you. The goat will not, she never thanks anybody.\nI have gone up in the boat with Ines Marlowe and that lovely old idiot Teo and his hen. Ines wants the Thalassa Mooring, the surface station, where the dive teams went down to the trench cables. She thinks the Network's divers saw where the children's shuttle drifted. I think she just wants to keep moving so she doesn't have to stop and think.\nThalassa still has a bell. If you go there, ring it carefully. Bells are loud, and you know now what loud does.\nLeave the lights off on your way out. Not because the Director says so. Because Wren does.
prop wrenletter obj.name=wrenletter
prop wrenletter beh.hidden=1
note rota Gardener's rota | BIOME SEVEN - ROTA (W. Ashby, gardener, staff of one)\n\nMon: melons. Tue: melons. Wed: the goat, who has opinions about Wednesdays. Thu: melons.\nFri: vent filters. Take the harpoon, the rays are back and they think the filters are a buffet.\nSat: crank the sprinklers. The valve sticks. Swear at it, it works better.\nSun: write to the Commons. They don't write back any more. Write to Sato. She does.\n\nAdded in red, last week: "Lights off after dark - by order of the Sealkeeper." Fine. Melons don't need the lights. I do, a bit.
note controldesk Control desk chest | The control desk's chest: engine control plans, "for the shuttle".
note gardenlocker Gardener's locker | Wren's locker: firework plans and her good gloves.
note seedvault Seed vault | The seed vault: mango, pineapple, strawberry, banana, beets, potatoes.
note ventchest Vent shed chest | A chest in the vent shed: metal detector plans, a filter.
note gantrybox Gantry box | The gantry's box on the dome's cap: zipline plans.
loot controldesk Blueprint_EngineControls*1;Bolt*2
prop controldesk loot.refill=0
loot gardenlocker Blueprint_Firework*1;Leather*1
prop gardenlocker loot.refill=0
loot seedvault Seed_Mango*2;Seed_Pineapple*2;Seed_Strawberry*2;Seed_Banana*2;Raw_Beet*3;Raw_Potato*3
prop seedvault loot.refill=0
loot ventchest Blueprint_MetalDetector*1;Scrap*2
prop ventchest loot.refill=0
loot gantrybox Blueprint_ZiplineBase*1;Rope*2
prop gantrybox loot.refill=0

